body:
[The documentation for the searchBox widget](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/documentation/#searchbox) says:

![unbenannt](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/36167/13920180/02668938-ef72-11e5-93bb-65a1ddfafbfd.PNG)

But how exactly must it be implemented? Does `queryHook` expect a (debounced) return? If so, what? object, function, bool? 

Calling a [debounce/deferr/throttle](https://code.openhub.net/file?fid=B6-cenRVoJ7qDbRegFtkguIsHY0&cid=uXtUw5YhiiU&s=&fp=305271&mp&projSelected=true#L0) function inside queryHook seems not to work.

```
    queryHook:function(query, search) {
        $.debounce(search(query), 1000);
        return false; // ? 
    }
```

comments.body:
You would do something like that:

``` js
    queryHook: $.debounce(function(query, search) {
      search(query);
    }, 1000);
```

Thanks for all the feedbacks and issues, much appreciated, really. We have a tutorial section #849 planned that would go deeper into cases like that.

This works! Thank you, @vvo !

```
queryHook: $.throttle(function(query, search) {
    query = query.replace(/\./, "");
    search(query);
}, 1000),
```
